A buffer the kernel refuses is no longer a NULL dereference (hakios, Redmi K40).

bo_new(): the process's cached buffers let go and the buffer asked for again, with pauses, for up to
30 s (said in the log through /dev/console); fd_bo_heap_alloc(): a heap block that could not be had gives
NULL, which bo_new() answers with a buffer of its own -- instead of fd_bo_mark_for_dump(NULL) at 0x18
(backboardd, 2026-11-02 00:01, work/TODO.md 2m). Made by work/wsl/mk-nomem-patch.py.

--- a/src/freedreno/drm/freedreno_bo.c
